    "description": "Job Description\n\nJob Summary\n\nCognex Corporation is seeking a highly skilled and experienced Senior Optical Design Engineer to lead the design, development, and optimization of advanced optical systems for our cutting-edge machine vision products. This role involves full lifecycle optical engineering, from conceptualization and simulation to prototyping, testing, and manufacturing support.\n\nJob Responsibilities\n\n* Lead the design and development of complex optical systems for industrial machine vision applications, including lenses, illumination modules, and sensor interfaces.\n* Utilize optical design software---Zemax, for system modeling, simulation, analysis, and tolerancing.\n* Conduct feasibility studies, trade-off analyses, and detailed performance predictions for new optical architectures.\n* Collaborate closely with mechanical, electrical, and software engineering teams to ensure seamless integration of optical designs into overall product architecture.\n* Specify, evaluate, and select optical components, materials, and manufacturing processes.\n* Develop and execute optical validation and verification test plans, including setting up optical benches and performing critical measurements.\n* Troubleshoot and resolve optical performance issues throughout the product development cycle and into production.\n\nJob Qualifications\n\n* Bachelor or above in Optical Engineering, or a related field.\n* 5+ years of professional experience in optical design and engineering, preferably in industrial or scientific imaging, machine vision, or a related high-tech industry.\n* Expert proficiency with industry-standard optical design software, Zemax is preferred.\n* Strong understanding of imaging optics, illumination principles, lens design, stray light analysis, and optical coatings.\n* Demonstrated experience with the full product development lifecycle, from concept to mass production.\n* Hands-on experience with optical lab equipment, alignment procedures, and metrology tools.\n* Familiarity with common optical manufacturing processes and their impact on design and tolerancing.\n* Excellent problem-solving skills, with a methodical and analytical approach to complex technical challenges.\n* Strong communication skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to clearly present technical information to diverse audiences.\n* Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, collaborative team environment.\n\nAdditional Job Description",
